{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"addf546344a983b8","type":"text","text":"[[Melvain.canvas]]\n#Melonia \n","x":-1000,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"fc27eecc24085148","x":-1000,"y":-320,"width":600,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"The Looking-Glass Plaza (Arrival Point):\nThe ground-level entry point into Melvain. A wide, bustling cobblestone square lined with dozens of massive mirrors. This is where the party will see students shoving luggage through the glass and vanishing, only to appear walking upside-down or high above on a translucent road.\n\nNPC: Barnaby, an Awakened Luggage Trunk (a domesticated mimic) who works as a bellhop, happily eating copper coins in exchange for carrying heavy bags through the mirrors.\n"},
		{"id":"563b0cf644cae727","x":-220,"y":-320,"width":657,"height":221,"type":"text","text":"The Crooked Hearth (Cafe & Social Hub):\nA cozy, crowded, Hogsmeade-style tavern perched on a translucent intersection high above the city. The entire building is physically tilted at a jagged 15-degree angle, but the localized gravity inside is perfectly flat. They serve smoking \"Levitating Lattes\" and spiced tarts.\n\nNPC: Madam Vesta, a fiery and chaotic Fire Genasi who literally uses her own hair to heat the espresso cauldrons and ovens.\n"},
		{"id":"6f566f5c7a446320","x":-1000,"y":20,"width":560,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"Thread & Aether (Magical Tailor):\nA high-end clothing shop crammed with floating mannequins. They specialize in weaving the local elements into clothing, selling cloaks that constantly gently billow without wind, or coats that radiate a permanent, comfortable warmth.\n\nNPC: Garrick, a flamboyant Half-Elf tailor whose measuring tapes are animated and slither around customers like friendly, inquisitive snakes to get exact measurements.\n"},
		{"id":"bd1694cc3174aa13","x":-220,"y":-10,"width":640,"height":230,"type":"text","text":"The Hanging Ward (Residential):\nA neighborhood of warm, Tudor-style homes suspended completely upside down on the underside of a higher district's translucent road. Residents use personalized gravity-boots or localized enchantments to walk \"normally\" to their front doors.\n\nNPC: Old Man Tock, a grumpy Clockwork Sorcerer who constantly walks around the neighborhood with a massive wrench, smacking the stone to recalibrate the gravity wards so the houses don't fall.\n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}